{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgAox92xz1Nrjp3m9qtDH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014KGo78iAUJwU9K7sPHhLMy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'E'\np='scripts/deploy.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='aws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\\n'\nnew='''# Short cache for everything outside assets/ (HTML, JS, CSS: unhashed names,\n# so browsers must revalidate soon). Excluded paths are also left alone by --delete.\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --exclude \"assets/*\" \\\\\n  --cache-control \"public, max-age=300, must-revalidate\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\n# Long cache for assets/ (logo, images).\naws s3 sync src/assets/ \"s3://$BUCKET/assets/\" --delete \\\\\n  --cache-control \"public, max-age=31536000\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n'''\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\nbash -n scripts/deploy.sh && cat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Cache-Control on deploy\n\nChanged `scripts/deploy.sh` (the single `aws s3 sync` is now two):\n\n- Everything except `assets/` (HTML, `booking.js`, `styles.css`):\n  `Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate` (5 minutes).\n- `assets/`: `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000` (1 year).\n\nNotes:\n- `styles.css` wasn't named in the request; I put it in the short group since its\n  filename isn't versioned and a stale stylesheet would have the same problem.\n- Assets have a long cache but unversioned names, so if you replace `logo.png`\n  in place, visitors may keep the old one for a long time. Rename the file\n  (or lower the value) when changing one.\n- `--exclude \"assets/*\"` on the first sync also stops `--delete` from touching\n  assets; the second sync handles deletion there.\n- Existing objects only get the header when re-uploaded. `s3 sync` skips files\n  whose size/mtime are unchanged, so the first deploy may not update metadata\n  for unchanged files. Force it once with `--exact-timestamps` is not enough; use\n  `aws s3 cp src/ s3://BUCKET/ --recursive --cache-control ...` (or touch the files).\n- Browsers that already cached `booking.js` with no header may still use their\n  heuristic copy until it expires; this only fixes future loads.\n- Not run: no deploy, and only `bash -n` syntax check was done.\nE"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":586,"cache_read_input_tokens":20416,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":586},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"6078a15b-bfb9-4d28-b456-d332e5888803","uuid":"15fd2df8-d4ba-479b-b941-bbc4f45f75a1","timestamp":"2026-10-19T02:31:03.244Z","request_id":"req_011CgAox8iNErmUW2VK4MXVH","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_014KGo78iAUJwU9K7sPHhLMy":{"command":"cd /private/tmp/h-AV2GCR && python3 - <<'E'\np='scripts/deploy.sh'\ns=open(p).read()\nold='aws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --profile \"$PROFILE\"\\n'\nnew='''# Short cache for everything outside assets/ (HTML, JS, CSS: unhashed names,\n# so browsers must revalidate soon). Excluded paths are also left alone by --delete.\naws s3 sync src/ \"s3://$BUCKET/\" --delete --exclude \"assets/*\" \\\\\n  --cache-control \"public, max-age=300, must-revalidate\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n\n# Long cache for assets/ (logo, images).\naws s3 sync src/assets/ \"s3://$BUCKET/assets/\" --delete \\\\\n  --cache-control \"public, max-age=31536000\" --profile \"$PROFILE\"\n'''\nassert old in s\nopen(p,'w').write(s.replace(old,new))\nE\nbash -n scripts/deploy.sh && cat > ANSWER.md <<'E'\n# Cache-Control on deploy\n\nChanged `scripts/deploy.sh` (the single `aws s3 sync` is now two):\n\n- Everything except `assets/` (HTML, `booking.js`, `styles.css`):\n  `Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate` (5 minutes).\n- `assets/`: `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000` (1 year).\n\nNotes:\n- `styles.css` wasn't named in the request; I put it in the short group since its\n  filename isn't versioned and a stale stylesheet would have the same problem.\n- Assets have a long cache but unversioned names, so if you replace `logo.png`\n  in place, visitors may keep the old one for a long time. Rename the file\n  (or lower the value) when changing one.\n- `--exclude \"assets/*\"` on the first sync also stops `--delete` from touching\n  assets; the second sync handles deletion there.\n- Existing objects only get the header when re-uploaded. `s3 sync` skips files\n  whose size/mtime are unchanged, so the first deploy may not update metadata\n  for unchanged files. Force it once with `--exact-timestamps` is not enough; use\n  `aws s3 cp src/ s3://BUCKET/ --recursive --cache-control ...` (or touch the files).\n- Browsers that already cached `booking.js` with no header may still use their\n  heuristic copy until it expires; this only fixes future loads.\n- Not run: no deploy, and only `bash -n` syntax check was done.\nE"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_014KGo78iAUJwU9K7sPHhLMy":{"cwd":"/private/tmp/h-AV2GCR"}}}
